# TableOfContents

## Purpose
Auto-collapsing article navigation with indigo links. Discover article headings, strip emoji from labels, and group h3 items under h2 items internally; display only h2 anchors. Collapse after selection.

## Configuration
Static HTML has no props. Use these equivalent inputs:

| Prop | Type | Default | HTML equivalent |
|---|---|---|---|
| `items` (required) | `TocItem[]` | — | Derive from article h2/h3 headings with unique IDs |
| `title` | string | `Contents` | `<summary>` text |
| `ariaLabel` | string | `Table of contents` | Navigation `aria-label` |
| `className` | string | — | Additional wrapper classes |
| `activeId` | string | — | Wrapper `data-active-id` |
| `onItemClick` | `(id: string) => void` | — | Listen for `toc-item-click`; `event.detail` is the ID |

`TocItem`: `{ id: string, label: string, level: 2 | 3, children?: TocItem[] }`. Children contain grouped h3 items and are not rendered.

## Semantic Hints
`toc`, `table-of-contents`, `navigation`, `outline`, `contents`, `nav`, `page-nav`, `section-nav`, `sidebar-toc`

## Integration and Behavior
Place in the article TOC placeholder; a plain JavaScript initializer replaces ArticleEnhancer. Not normally authored inside article prose. Use a compact, muted title, indigo links, and bold active links. Intersection Observer tracks sections. Native anchors support keyboard navigation; a polite status announces changes. Respect reduced-motion preferences.

## Complete Example
Save as `article.html`.

```html
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
<title>Article</title>
<style>
html{scroll-behavior:smooth}
.toc{max-width:20rem;font: .9rem system-ui}
summary{color:#555;font-weight:600}
.toc ul{padding-left:1.2rem}
.toc a{color:#4338ca;text-decoration:none}
.toc a[aria-current]{font-weight:bold}
.toc a:focus-visible{outline:2px solid}
.sr{position:absolute;clip-path:inset(50%);width:1px;height:1px;overflow:hidden}
section{min-height:80vh}
@media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){html{scroll-behavior:auto}}
</style>
<body>
<details class="toc" open data-active-id="start">
<summary>Contents</summary>
<nav aria-label="Table of contents"><ul></ul></nav>
</details>
<p class="sr" role="status"></p>
<article>
<section><h2 id="start">🚀 Introduction</h2><p>Welcome.</p>
<h3 id="requirements">Requirements</h3><p>A browser.</p></section>
<section><h2 id="next">Next steps</h2><p>Continue reading.</p></section>
</article>
<script>
const toc=document.querySelector('.toc'), items=[];
document.querySelectorAll('article h2,article h3').forEach(h=>{
 const item={id:h.id,label:h.textContent.replace(
 /[\p{Extended_Pictographic}\p{Emoji_Modifier}\uFE0F\u200D]/gu,''
 ).trim(),level:Number(h.tagName[1])};
 if(item.level===2)items.push(item);
 else if(items.length)(items.at(-1).children??=[]).push(item);
});
const links=items.map(item=>{
 const li=document.createElement('li'),a=document.createElement('a');
 a.href='#'+item.id;
 a.textContent=item.label;
 li.append(a);
 toc.querySelector('ul').append(li);
 a.addEventListener('click',()=>{
  activate(item.id);
  toc.open=false;
  toc.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent('toc-item-click',{detail:item.id}));
 });
 return a;
});
function activate(id){
 links.forEach((a,i)=>{
  if(items[i].id===id)a.setAttribute('aria-current','true');
  else a.removeAttribute('aria-current');
 });
 document.querySelector('[role=status]').textContent=
 items.find(i=>i.id===id)?.label||'';
}
activate(toc.dataset.activeId);
const observer=new IntersectionObserver(entries=>{
 entries.forEach(e=>{if(e.isIntersecting)activate(e.target.id)});
},{rootMargin:'0px 0px -60% 0px'});
items.forEach(i=>observer.observe(document.getElementById(i.id)));
</script>
</body>
</html>
```

framework_component_specs.ArticleCardBySlug:
# ArticleCardBySlug

## Purpose
An HTML card populated by JavaScript from an article registry using a slug. Resolves metadata, formats dates, resolves authors, and supplies a fallback image. Without JavaScript, the empty card containers remain hidden.

## Inputs
Use HTML `data-*` attributes instead of component props.

| Prop | HTML attribute | Type | Default | Description |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `slug` (required) | `data-slug` | string | — | Article registry slug |
| `ctaText` | `data-cta-text` | string | `Read more` | CTA link text |
| `className` | `class` | string | — | Additional CSS classes |
| `descriptionOverride` | `data-description-override` | string | — | Replacement description |
| `variant` | `data-variant` | `default` or `compact` | `default` | Card size |
| `authorOverride` | `data-author-override` | Author JSON | — | Replacement author |

`Author` is an object with a `name` string. Encode JSON safely inside the attribute.

## Semantic Hints
`card`, `article-card`, `slug-card`, `dynamic-card`, `registry-card`, `auto-card`

## When to Use
Use when a slug should determine the card content without duplicating article metadata. Static HTML has no native registry lookup; the script below performs it in the browser. No framework imports are required.

## Behavior and Styling
Look up the slug, resolve metadata and author, apply overrides, format the date, and render semantic ArticleCard markup. Reuse ArticleCard styles through `.article-card`; use `[data-variant="compact"]` for compact styling. This wrapper needs no additional styles.

For an unknown slug, log a warning and leave the container hidden, rendering nothing.

## Complete Example
Save as `index.html`. Registry entries are illustrative; replace them with project metadata. Repeat containers to create a grid.

```html
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>Articles</title>
</head>
<body>
  <div class="article-grid">
    <article class="article-card" data-slug="machine-learning-basics" hidden></article>
    <article class="article-card" data-slug="ai-in-healthcare"
      data-variant="compact" data-cta-text="Explore"
      data-description-override="Custom description for this context"
      data-author-override='{"name":"Guest author"}' hidden></article>
  </div>

  <template id="article-card">
    <img alt="">
    <h2><a></a></h2>
    <p class="description"></p>
    <p><span class="author"></span> · <time></time></p>
    <a class="cta"></a>
  </template>

  <script>
    const authors = { editor: { name: "Editorial team" } };
    const articles = {
      "machine-learning-basics": {
        title: "Machine Learning Basics",
        description: "An introduction to machine learning.",
        date: "2025-01-15", author: "editor"
      },
      "ai-in-healthcare": {
        title: "AI in Healthcare", description: "AI in practice.",
        date: "2025-02-01", author: "editor"
      }
    };
    const fallback = "data:image/svg+xml," +
      encodeURIComponent('<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="640" height="360"><rect width="100%" height="100%" fill="#eee"/></svg>');

    document.querySelectorAll("[data-slug]").forEach(card => {
      const d = card.dataset;
      const article = articles[d.slug];
      if (!article) {
        console.warn("Unknown article slug:", d.slug);
        return;
      }
      const author = d.authorOverride
        ? JSON.parse(d.authorOverride)
        : authors[article.author] || article.author;
      card.append(document.querySelector("#article-card").content.cloneNode(true));
      const find = selector => card.querySelector(selector);
      find("img").src = article.image || fallback;
      find("img").onerror = event => {
        event.target.onerror = null;
        event.target.src = fallback;
      };
      find("h2 a").textContent = article.title;
      find(".description").textContent = d.descriptionOverride ?? article.description;
      find(".author").textContent = author?.name || "";
      find("time").dateTime = article.date;
      find("time").textContent = new Date(article.date + "T00:00:00Z")
        .toLocaleDateString("en", { dateStyle: "medium", timeZone: "UTC" });
      card.querySelectorAll("a").forEach(link => {
        link.href = "/articles/" + encodeURIComponent(d.slug) + "/";
      });
      find(".cta").textContent = d.ctaText ?? "Read more";
      card.hidden = false;
    });
  </script>
</body>
</html>
```

