# ArticleDisclaimer

## Purpose
Full-width, pill-shaped disclaimer banner with an icon, dark background, and light text. Use for legal disclaimers, regulatory notices, or important caveats near the top or bottom of articles containing legal, financial, or medical content.

## Configuration
Static HTML uses markup rather than component props. No configuration is required; use the default markup below.

| Original prop | HTML equivalent | Type | Default | Description |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `className` | Additional values in `class` | string | None | Append CSS classes to the banner. |
| `message` | Paragraph text | string | “This article is for informational purposes only and does not constitute professional advice.” | Replace with a custom disclaimer. |
| `icon` | Inline SVG or other icon markup | HTML | Lightbulb SVG | Replace the decorative icon; retain `aria-hidden="true"`. |
| `linkText` | Anchor text | string | None | Optional link label. |
| `linkHref` | Anchor `href` | URL string | None | Optional destination URL. Include the anchor only when both link fields are supplied. |

## Semantic Hints
`disclaimer`, `notice`, `legal`, `warning`, `note`, `legal-notice`, `terms`, `advisory`

## Structure and Styling
- Banner contains a left icon, message, and optional right-side link.
- Fill the content width with comfortable padding and rounded corners.
- Use a dark background, contrasting light text, and text slightly smaller than body copy.
- Allow wrapping on narrow screens.

## Accessibility
Use `role="note"` for informational content; reserve `role="alert"` for critical, dynamically inserted notices. Maintain WCAG AA contrast. Hide decorative icons from assistive technology. If a link opens a new tab, state this in its label and use `rel="noopener noreferrer"`.

## Complete Example
Save as `article-disclaimer.html`. No imports or JavaScript required.

```html
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>Article disclaimer</title>
  <style>
    body { margin: 0; padding: 1rem; font-family: sans-serif; }
    .article-disclaimer {
      box-sizing: border-box;
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      gap: .75rem;
      width: 100%;
      padding: 1rem 1.5rem;
      border-radius: 1.5rem;
      background: #18181b;
      color: #fafafa;
      font-size: .875rem;
      line-height: 1.5;
    }
    .article-disclaimer svg { flex: none; }
    .article-disclaimer p { flex: 1 1 15rem; margin: 0; }
    .article-disclaimer a { color: inherit; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
    .article-disclaimer a:focus-visible {
      outline: 2px solid white;
      outline-offset: 4px;
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <div class="article-disclaimer" role="note">
    <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24"
         fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"
         aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
      <path d="M9 18h6M9 21h6M9 15c0-3-4-3-4-8a7 7 0 0 1 14 0c0 5-4 5-4 8Z"/>
    </svg>
    <p>This article is for informational purposes only and does not constitute professional advice.</p>
    <!-- Optional: remove this anchor for default usage. -->
    <a href="/legal/disclaimer">View our full disclaimer</a>
  </div>
</body>
</html>
```

