# ArticleReferences

## Purpose
Collapsible source list with category badges. Initially shows a preview; “Show all” reveals remaining references. Use at the end of research-heavy articles to establish credibility.

## Configuration
Static HTML has no props or imports. Edit the markup and attributes in `article-references.html`.

| Original prop | Type | Default | HTML equivalent |
|---|---|---|---|
| `references` (required) | `Reference[]` | — | One `<li>` per reference |
| `heading` | string | `References` | `<h2>` text |
| `description` | string | — | Optional paragraph below heading |
| `headingId` | string | `references` | Heading `id`; section `aria-labelledby` |
| `previewCount` | number | `5` | Nonnegative integer in `data-preview-count` |

### Reference fields
- `title`: required string; descriptive link text.
- `url`: required string; link `href`.
- `category`: optional `government`, `guide`, `analysis`, `industry`, `watchlist`, or `academic`; badge text and `data-category`.
- `author`: optional string; text following the title.
- `date`: optional string; use `<time datetime="YYYY-MM-DD">` for a machine-readable date.
- `description`: optional string; paragraph inside the item.

## Semantic Hints
`references`, `citations`, `sources`, `bibliography`, `footnotes`, `resources`, `external-links`, `sources-list`

## Structure and Behavior
Use a labelled section containing a heading, optional description, semantic list, and toggle button. Omit absent fields. Hide the toggle when all references fit the preview. Keep IDs unique when repeating the section.

Items need comfortable spacing and clear links. Badges are small pills: government blue, guide green, analysis purple, industry orange, watchlist red, academic indigo. Animate expansion; respect reduced motion. Links opening new tabs must announce this. The native button supports keyboard use and exposes `aria-expanded`.

## Working HTML Example
```html
<style>
.article-references li { margin-block: 1rem; }
.article-references small {
  display: inline-block; padding: .15rem .5rem;
  border-radius: 1rem; color: white;
}
[data-category="government"] { background: #164b9b; }
[data-category="guide"] { background: #176338; }
[data-category="analysis"] { background: #71349b; }
[data-category="industry"] { background: #943d08; }
[data-category="watchlist"] { background: #ac2020; }
[data-category="academic"] { background: #39358e; }
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) {
  .article-references .revealed { animation: reveal .25s ease; }
  @keyframes reveal { from { opacity: 0; } to { opacity: 1; } }
}
</style>

<section class="article-references" aria-labelledby="references"
  data-preview-count="1">
  <h2 id="references">Sources &amp; Further Reading</h2>
  <p>Sources used in researching this article.</p>
  <ul id="references-list">
    <li>
      <small data-category="government">Government</small>
      <a href="https://www.industry.gov.au/ai-ethics"
        target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Australian Government AI Ethics Framework ↗ (opens in new tab)</a>
    </li>
    <li>
      <small data-category="guide">Guide</small>
      <a href="https://ieee.org/ai-guidelines"
        target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">IEEE AI Guidelines ↗ (opens in new tab)</a>
      <p>Guidance for AI development.</p>
    </li>
  </ul>
  <button type="button" hidden aria-expanded="false"
    aria-controls="references-list">Show all references</button>
</section>

<script>
document.querySelectorAll('.article-references').forEach(section => {
  const items = [...section.querySelectorAll('li')];
  const extra = items.slice(Number(section.dataset.previewCount ?? 5));
  const button = section.querySelector('button');
  if (!extra.length) return;
  function update(open) {
    extra.forEach(item => {
      item.hidden = !open;
      item.classList.toggle('revealed', open);
    });
    button.setAttribute('aria-expanded', String(open));
    button.textContent = open ? 'Show fewer references'
      : `Show all ${items.length} references`;
  }
  update(false);
  button.hidden = false;
  button.addEventListener('click', () =>
    update(button.getAttribute('aria-expanded') !== 'true'));
});
</script>
```

