# ArticleTocPlaceholder

## Purpose
An empty `<div data-article-toc-placeholder>` that serves as the mounting point for a dynamically generated table of contents. In Static Html, an optional ArticleEnhancer script inserts DOM elements directly; no React Portal is required.

## Options
Static Html uses attributes and CSS classes rather than component props.

### Required
None.

### Optional
| Original prop | Type | Default | Static Html equivalent |
|---|---|---|---|
| `className` | `string` | — | Add CSS classes with `class`. |
| `noMargin` | `boolean` | `false` | Add `toc-placeholder--no-margin` to remove default margins. |

## Semantic Hints
`toc-placeholder`, `sidebar-toc`, `toc-wrapper`, `toc-slot`, `toc-container`

## When to Use
Place near the top of long articles or in a sidebar. The placeholder stays hidden unless ArticleEnhancer generates TOC links.

## Structure
```html
<div class="toc-placeholder" data-article-toc-placeholder hidden></div>
```
Keep the element empty in the source. The enhancer inserts a list of links targeting article headings with unique IDs.

## Behavior
1. Find the placeholder using `[data-article-toc-placeholder]`.
2. Collect article section headings with IDs.
3. Insert links using DOM methods.
4. Add navigation semantics and reveal the populated container.
5. If no headings qualify, leave it empty and hidden.

## Styling and Placement
- Use rounded borders, a subtle background, and a width matching the content area.
- **Sidebar:** place alongside the article; use sticky positioning on desktop.
- **Inline:** place before the first section, especially on mobile.
- **Floating:** use fixed positioning and an accessible toggle button.
- Hide empty placeholders to avoid visible decoration and empty navigation landmarks.

## Accessibility
When populated, set `role="navigation"` and `aria-label="Table of contents"`. Keep the empty container hidden. Links must target unique heading IDs.

## Complete Example
Save as `article.html`. This inline example removes default margins; omit the modifier class to restore them.

```html
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>Article with table of contents</title>
  <style>
    main { max-width: 48rem; margin: auto; padding: 1rem; }
    .toc-placeholder {
      margin: 1.5rem 0;
      padding: 1rem;
      border: 1px solid #ddd;
      border-radius: .5rem;
      background: #f7f7f7;
    }
    .toc-placeholder--no-margin { margin: 0; }
    .toc-placeholder[hidden] { display: none; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <main>
    <article>
      <h1>Article Title</h1>
      <div class="toc-placeholder toc-placeholder--no-margin"
           data-article-toc-placeholder hidden></div>
      <section>
        <h2 id="first-section">First Section</h2>
        <p>Article content.</p>
      </section>
    </article>
  </main>
  <script>
    function enhanceArticle() {
      const slot = document.querySelector('[data-article-toc-placeholder]');
      if (!slot) return;
      const headings = slot.closest('article').querySelectorAll('h2[id]');
      if (!headings.length) return;
      const list = document.createElement('ul');
      headings.forEach((heading) => {
        const item = document.createElement('li');
        const link = document.createElement('a');
        link.href = '#' + encodeURIComponent(heading.id);
        link.textContent = heading.textContent;
        item.append(link);
        list.append(item);
      });
      slot.replaceChildren(list);
      slot.setAttribute('role', 'navigation');
      slot.setAttribute('aria-label', 'Table of contents');
      slot.hidden = false;
    }
    enhanceArticle();
  </script>
</body>
</html>
```

